# Memcheck suppressions for the ARM64 unsafe-valgrind lanes only; the x86-64
# runner does not load this file. See docs/unsafe-validation.md.
#
# 2026-10-16: reedsolomon_rs::fft::add_tile::<u16>, called from
# transform_tiles_alone / transform_sum, reports "Conditional jump or move
# depends on uninitialised value(s)" on ARM64 in
# fft::tests::tiled_transforms_match_whole_row_sweeps (reedsolomon-rs) and
# fft::lane_tests::the_four_step_gate_does_not_change_a_byte and
# fft::lane_tests::the_byte_lane_matches_the_word_lane_bit_for_bit (par3-rs).
# Everything add_tile reads is initialised: `after` is a Vec<bool> cloned from
# a collected vector in sweep_flags, and the tile views and `sum` are rows of
# RowBank::zeroed (alloc_zeroed or a zeroed anonymous mapping) or collected
# Vecs; neither crate's FFT uses set_len, MaybeUninit or a read of
# with_capacity spare space. The same tests pass under x86-64 Memcheck and
# under AddressSanitizer on both architectures, so this is Memcheck's ARM64
# definedness tracking, not an uninitialised read. Remove this entry when a
# newer Valgrind passes those tests without it.
{
   reedsolomon-fft-add-tile-aarch64-cond
   Memcheck:Cond
   fun:*add_tile*
}
